title: The <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> joins the <span style="color: #BFC8CC;">**GNU**</span>
subtitle: The miniscule party can no longer survive on its own.
view-if: chancellor = "Staal" and staal_time >= 35 and republicans_staal >= 12 and not lvp_formed and ddp_r < 2 and gnu_formed
new-page: true
priority: 1
tags: event
max-visits: 1

= <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> joins the <span style="color: #BFC8CC;">**GNU**</span>

With the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> effectively dead as a political force, many former politicians—especially on its right wing—have long advocated for its self-dissolution, believing only then could a new, unified force rise from its ashes.

That belief has only strengthened with the rise of the <span style="color: #BFC8CC;">**GNU**</span>. Now, more party members are calling for a formal merger into Staal's organization. His appeals to national unity have struck a psychological blow to the rank and file of a party that always championed the welfare and unity of the nation as a whole above all.

Old-line <span style="color: #D3C24D;">democrats</span> like Dietrich and Hewes remain the most resistant, committed <span style="color: #000000;">repu</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">bli</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">cans</span> to the core. But figures like Lemmer and the party’s left wing are proving more susceptible to Staal’s calls for national unity.

Nonetheless, a vote is conducted, and the opposition wins.

- @schleicher_2: The <span style="color: #BFC8CC;">Commonwealth National Unity Front</span> welcomes its new member.

@schleicher_2
on-arrival: {!
Q.dstp_gnu = 1

Q.pro_republic -= Q.ddp_votes;

Q.ddp_relation = Q.gnu_relation;

Q.gnu_r += Q.ddp_r;
Q.ddp_r = 0;

if (Q.ddp_ideology == "Left") Q.ddp_leader = "Lemmer";
if (Q.ddp_ideology != "Left") Q.ddp_leader = "Hellpach";

Q.old_ddp_name = Q.ddp_name;
Q.ddp_name = "DStP";
!}

Staal sees keeping the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ old_ddp_name +]**</span> as a separate but closely tied <i>bloc party</i> as more effective in attracting voters, and for now, maintains their nominal independence[? if not dstp_formed:, though under a new name to shed the old and ironic "Democratic" label?]. [+ ddp_leader +] has since been installed as leader of the now <i>bloc party</i>-aligned <span style="color: #D3C24D;">[+ ddp_name +]</span>.

Current composition of the <span style="color: #BFC8CC;">Commonwealth National Unity Front</span>:

[? if gnu_formed: - <span style="color: #BFC8CC;">**GNU**</span> ?]

[? if dstp_gnu: - <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> ?]

[? if lvp_gnu: - <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> ?]

[? if unionist_gnu: - <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> ?]

[? if unionist_gnu: - <span style="color: #A2D8E0;">**Arcanists**</span> ?]

[? if gold_gnu: - <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> ?]

[? if other_gnu: - **Others** ?]

[? if kvp_gnu: - <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span> ?]

[? if traditionalist_gnu: - <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> ?]

[? if nvf_gnu: - <span style="color: #142e20;">**NVF**</span> ?]